#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:3
#: 3d3b95b346564ac09b72806dad64e77f
msgid "Safe remote dom0 terminals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:6
#: f96877c3df454b40a2853c5f5fa98282
msgid ""
"If you do not have working graphics in Dom0, then using a terminal can be "
"quite annoying! This was the case for the author while trying to debug PCI-"
"passthrough of a machine’s primary (only) GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:8
#: 7e1b850d33464cc2b6fa2a9d082c27c8
msgid ""
"Your first thought might be to just allow network access to Dom0, enable "
"ssh, and connect in remotely. But, this gravely violates the Qubes security "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:10
#: 3baa9dc5c37c4e4ab8c5d792362c97ea
msgid ""
"Instead, a better solution is to split the input and output paths of using a "
"terminal. Use your normal keyboard for input, but have the output go to a "
"remote machine in a unidirectional manner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:12
#: f3f6e274436d471d87ad0dde4a7d25cd
msgid ""
"To do this, we make use of script(1), qvm-run, and optionally your network "
"transport of choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:15
#: e9fd05a193cd49d09ef268c3c3a2e892
msgid "To a different VM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:18
#: 247f3e25335a444faed70f6546784906
msgid ""
"As an example of forwarding terminal output to another VM on the same "
"machine:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:29
#: 905d92451bcb406f923834fb385b1da6
msgid "To a different machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:32
#: 1ce47f202fea4e4392cd3ccc01c80b28
msgid "In this case over SSH (from a network-connected VM):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:44
#: ba7fe2f360014078b08793c8b9b004fc
msgid ""
"Note that no data received over SSH is ever treated as terminal input in "
"Dom0. The input path remains only from your trusted local keyboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:47
#: 9af456ab158145dfb9c71e4bbbd671e2
msgid "Multiple terminals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:50
#: 74bd90fe32884d549d34da72fe943b05
msgid ""
"For multiple terminals, you may find it easier to just use tmux than to try "
"to blindly switch to the correct window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:53
#: 3a732c75e5b54998bd182118fb5dbdd9
msgid "Terminal size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:56
#: 3d8e70e755eb4207b2c23e7475fc8638
msgid ""
"It is up to you to ensure the sizes of the local and remote terminal are the "
"same, otherwise things may display incorrectly (especially in interactive "
"programs). Depending on your shell, the size of your local (blind) terminal "
"is likely stored in the ``$LINES`` and ``$COLUMNS`` variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:66
#: 89a771d160594d7d8a86a8f737849e86
msgid "A note on serial consoles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:69
#: 45b3ebc759f74c328b64589dc0fd4f7d
msgid ""
"If your machine has a serial console, you may with to use that, but note "
"that a similar split-I/O model should be used to ensure Dom0 integrity. If "
"you use the serial console as normal (via e.g. getty on ttyX, and logging in "
"as normal), then the machine at the end of the serial cable could compromise "
"your machine! Ideally, you would take input from your trusted keyboard, and "
"only send the output over the serial cable via e.g. disabling getty and "
"using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../developer/debugging/safe-remote-ttys.rst:77
#: 77d46445812143d5b35afc9e09fcd071
msgid "You don’t even need to connect the TX pin."
msgstr ""
